                        <h4 class="mb-4">Introduction</h4>
                        <p>Your <b>Traffic Cop</b> is a multifunctional tool primarily designed to collect data about the visitor traffic to your parcel or region. While data collection is it's primary purpose, since it is already
                        monitoring visitors, we also gave it Security and Greeting functionality. As part of the greeting functionality, it can greet first time and returning visitors differently as well as give an item such as a landmark or
                        welcome package to your visitors. This can reduce the number of scripted objects you use, reducing lag.</p>
                        
                        <p>Your Traffic Cop can be turned on and off, and you can inactivate the greeting and security functions. It can also function on group owned land.</p>

                        <h4 class="mt-5">Usage</h4>

                        <h5 class="mt-4">Setup</h5>
                        <p>To start using a traffic cop, first rez it. You should rename it, especially if you are using multiple traffic cops. Touch it, then choose <b>Reset</b> from the dialog menu.</p>
                        
                        <p>In it's default state, a traffic cop is powered off. To turn it on, choose <b>Sensor On</b> from the menu. Once powered on, the object will
                        start scanning every 30 seconds and sending data about visitors to the database. Additionally, the unit must be powered on for security and greeting
                        functionality.</p> 
                        
                        
                        <h5 class="mt-4">Settings</h5>
                        
                        <h6 class="mt-3">Linking a Server and Inventory</h6>
                        <p>You only need to link a <b>Server</b> if you want your traffic cop to give visitors inventory. To link a server and inventory to give, you will first need to rez a server and put 
                        the inventory you desire into the server's contents. You can get instructions how to do that <%= link_to 'here', static_pages_docs_servers_path %>. You can link to a server via the web site or 
                        from the traffic cop.</p>
                        
                        <p>To link a server and inventory from the website, go to the page for your traffic cop and click the edit button. First link the desired server by choosing it from the dropdown list then
                        hitting <b>Update Traffic cop</b>. Edit the traffic cop again, then choose the inventory you desire, then click <b>Update Traffic cop</b>.</p>
                        
                        <p>Linking from the object itself follows a similar workflow. First chose <b>Server</b> from the dialog menu, then choose the desired server. Then click the <b>Inventory</b> button and 
                        choose the desired inventory. If you do not want the traffic cop to give anything, just leave the inventory unset.</p>
            
                        
